{
  "id": "proj-kids-step-stool",
  "slug": "kids-step-stool",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Kids' Step Stool",
  "summary": "A two-step stool with hand-hold cutouts. Small enough to finish before the glue in your last project dries.",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "estimatedHours": 2,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Cut the 1x12 into two 14 in sides, a 16 in top tread, a 16 in lower tread and a 16 in back stretcher, then rip both treads to 7 in wide.",
    "Draw the stepped profile on one side (lower step 6 in high and 7 in deep, top 12 in high), cut it with the jigsaw, then trace it onto the second side and cut that.",
    "Below the top step on each side, drill two 1 in holes 4 in apart with the spade bit and jigsaw out the waste between them to make a hand-hold slot.",
    "Glue and screw the treads and back stretcher between the sides with countersunk 1 1/4 in screws. Check the stool for square and for rocking on a flat floor before the glue sets.",
    "Fill the screw holes, sand to 180 grit and round every edge, then brush on three coats of water-based polyurethane. Let it cure for a week, then add the non-slip tape to the treads and rubber feet underneath."
  ],
